*Drawing to be made by the candidate: a longitudinal section through a joint such as the knee or the elbow (e.g. a ball and socket or hinge joint), titled "Section through a synovial joint".*

**Elements to draw and label:**

- the **two bones** meeting at the joint (the ends of the bones are rounded or hollowed);
- **articular (hyaline) cartilage** covering the end of each bone (smooth, reduces friction and absorbs shock);
- **synovial fluid** filling the **synovial (joint) cavity** between the cartilages (lubricates the joint);
- **synovial membrane** lining the capsule and secreting the synovial fluid;
- **joint capsule (fibrous capsule)** enclosing the joint, together with **ligaments** that join bone to bone and keep the bones in place;
- (optionally) a **tendon** joining a muscle to a bone.
